    "narrative": "Today\u2019s roster for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by a high-upside trio in **Seiya Suzuki** (75.03), **Josh Naylor** (75.33), and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92). **Seiya Suzuki** holds our top mark due to a rare convergence of an elite BvP history (28 PA) against Lodolo and a favorable park factor, while **Josh Naylor** benefits from the highest SP_xERA of the day (5.92) as he faces Quintana. Despite facing tough arms in Schlittler, **Corbin Carroll** and **Gabriel Moreno** remain in the lineup; **Corbin Carroll**\u2019s elite sprint speed remains essential to our 5x5 pursuit of stolen bases, even as his efficiency is suppressed by the matchup. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** (71.55) is an absolute must-start today, as the 14% park boost combined with the stolen base opportunity against a slow-delivery pitcher makes him a primary driver for our scarce SB category.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was benching **Austin Riley** (57.09), who was the first player left out despite a solid score. While **Austin Riley** offers stability, the optimizer preferred the specialized upside of **Jose Caballero** and **Mickey Moniak** due to their situational speed utility. We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Brice Turang**, who is currently listed as a bench option; his elite potential for SB production is neutralized today by his removal from the confirmed starting lineup, effectively zeroing his efficiency contribution. Owners should note that **Giancarlo Stanton** and **Tyler Soderstrom** remain sidelined on the IL, leaving us reliant on the depth provided by **Max Muncy**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Cole Young** to manage our game caps down the stretch. **James Wood** (67.71) rounds out our strongest plays, bolstered by an elite 0.412 xwOBA and the leadoff spot against McGreevy, making him a high-floor asset in a pivotal divisional matchup.",
